10378 | Page 236 | {} | 4. P. M. 2nd / Via Ft Monroe & Yorktown June 2nd  / Near Bethsaida Church 5 P. M. June 1st. For Secy War Washington / Sheridan Successfully held his position at Cold Harbor repulsing an / attack of part of Longstreets Corps this morning , the  / advance of the 6th corps got to Cold Harbor at 9 am / . Wrights Column was closely followed by Smiths , Wright  / was ordered to attack the enemy at once but reconnoitered / skirmished & delayed till he found at 2 P. M. that there / were no longer any rebels before him . It appears  / however that they still had a part of the road between  / Bethsaida Church & Cold Harbor . I reported in  / my dispatch of 10 Warren was ordered to attack a / Column of rebel Infantry which was passing towards Cold Harbor / but instead of falling upon it in force he opened / with Artillery & at 3 P. M reported that the Entrenchments  / of the Enemy were exceedingly strong & that his own lines / were so long that he had no mass of troops / to attack with . It seems that Wright blundered in the  / execution of his order to march to Cold Harbor , / instead of having his advance there at 9 am , it / was <insertion>Gen</insertion> Grants & Meades design that his whole corps should / be on the ground at day light , then a / rapid attack in mass would certainly have routed the rebel / force which a little later assaulted Sheridan and an / advantage might easily have been gained which followed up / by Sheridan two divisions of Cavalry might have led to / the disposal of Lee's Army . Both Gen Grant and Meade's / 
